### 1.3 CHIPS Act Programs (NIST, CHIPS R&D Office)

The CHIPS and Science Act of 2022 provided $50B to Commerce, with $11B directed to the CHIPS R&D Office.

**CHIPS Metrology SBIR Program — Most relevant to a startup**
In April 2024, CHIPS for America announced a **$54M SBIR funding opportunity** specifically targeting small businesses for semiconductor measurement services, tools, and instrumentation:
- Phase I awards: up to $283,500
- Phase II awards: up to $1,910,000
- In September 2024, ~$5M was awarded to 17 small businesses across 9 states, all eligible for Phase II in Spring 2025
- Topics include: measurement services for semiconductor manufacturing, novel **assurance and provenance technologies**, and advanced metrology R&D testbeds

**The "assurance and provenance technologies" subtopic is directly applicable to post-silicon validation and failure analysis.**

Sources: [NIST announcement](https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2024/04/chips-america-announces-over-50-million-funding-opportunity-encourage-small) | [NIST FAQ](https://www.nist.gov/chips/frequently-asked-questions-chips-metrology-sbir-funding-opportunity) | [NIST awards](https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2024/09/biden-harris-administration-awards-nearly-5-million-small-businesses-bring)

**CHIPS Manufacturing USA Institute** — January 2025, SRC awarded $285M to build an institute focused on digital twins for semiconductor manufacturing and **validation of those digital twins** in a physical prototyping facility. Digital twin validation is directly adjacent to post-silicon validation tooling.

Source: [Federal Register](https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2024/02/01/2024-02025/chips-manufacturing-usa-institute)

**CHIPS BAA 2025** — September 2025, CHIPS R&D Office released BAA No. 2025-NIST-CHIPS-CRDO-01.

Source: [Inside Government Contracts](https://www.insidegovernmentcontracts.com/2025/11/u-s-department-of-commerce-opens-new-funding-opportunity-for-semiconductor-rd/)

