### 1.4 DoD Trusted Foundry Programs (DMEA / TAPO / AFRL)

DMEA's **Trusted Access Program Office (TAPO)** accredits suppliers across the full semiconductor supply chain including **test services**. An active research paper (2024/2025) describes a workflow for "Applying a Trusted Microelectronics Post-Silicon Verification & Validation Workflow to Legacy Integrated Circuit Design Recovery" — indicating funded work at the intersection of DMEA and post-silicon validation.

The **Air Force Research Laboratory (AFRL)** ran the **Assured and Trusted Microelectronics Solutions (ATMS)** program explicitly listing research interests in:
- Embedded ASIC structures to assist in post-fabrication analysis
- Non-destructive test techniques
- Algorithms to reduce analysis time
- **Fusion technologies capitalizing on multiple data sets**

Battelle won $16.6M in AFRL contracts for microelectronics security work.

Sources: [DMEA Trusted Supplier Program](https://www.acq.osd.mil/asds/dmea/tapo/trusted-supplier-programs.html) | [Post-Silicon V&V paper](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/387116620_Applying_a_Trusted_Microelectronics_Post-Silicon_Verification_Validation_Workflow_to_Legacy_Integrated_Circuit_Design_Recovery) | [Battelle AFRL](https://www.battelle.org/insights/newsroom/press-release-details/battelle-team-wins-16.6-million-in-contract-awards-for-microelectronics-security-from-air-force-research-laboratory)

