### 1.5 SBIR/STTR Opportunities

**SBIR Reauthorization Status:** Authorization expired September 30, 2025. The Senate passed reauthorization unanimously on March 3, 2026; House passed March 17, 2026, extending programs through **FY2031**. New solicitations are expected to resume imminently.

**DARPA Microsystems Exploration (μE):**
- Awards up to $2M, 24 months
- Open rolling solicitation, DARPA-PA-25-01: October 2024–October 2025
- Uses OTA structure (lower overhead)
- DARPA commits to notifying proposers within 90 days

Source: [simpler.grants.gov](https://simpler.grants.gov/opportunity/354134)

**NSF SBIR Semiconductors:**
Subtopics include Integrated Circuit Design (S3), Processing and Metrology Technology (S6), and Novel Semiconductor-based Sensors (S5).
- Phase I: ~$300K
- Phase II: up to $1.25M

Source: [NSF SBIR Semiconductors](https://seedfund.nsf.gov/topics/semiconductors/)

**DARPA TTO BAA 2025 (HR001125S0011):**
Includes a "Design/Build/Buy" focus area calling for "new approaches to testing and validation that dramatically shorten the timeline from initial delivery to full military utility." Proposals accepted rolling through June 22, 2026.

Source: [SAM.gov TTO BAA](https://sam.gov/opp/109aceb76198452b91f8ecce72b4890b/view)

