## Summary: Key Funding Vehicles for a Silicon Reliability / Post-Silicon Validation Startup

| Program | Agency | Relevance | Award Size | Startup Access |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| CHIPS Metrology SBIR | NIST/Commerce | **Direct** — assurance, provenance tools | Phase I ~$283K; Phase II ~$1.9M | **High** — open SBIR |
| DARPA Microsystems Exploration (μE) | DARPA MTO | Medium — novel microsystems incl. test/validation | Up to $2M, 24 months | **High** — rolling OTA |
| DARPA ASSERT | DARPA MTO | **Direct** — radiation testing of advanced electronics | ~$10–18M/performer | Low — prime contracts |
| DARPA SBIR (quarterly) | DARPA | Variable by topic | Phase I ~$250K; Phase II ~$1.8M | **High** — open SBIR |
| NSF SBIR (Semiconductors) | NSF | IC design, metrology, sensors | Phase I ~$300K; Phase II ~$1.25M | **High** — open SBIR |
| DARPA TTO BAA 2025 | DARPA TTO | Medium — testing/validation in defense context | Variable ~$1–5M | Medium — full proposal |
| AFRL ATMS / Trusted Microelectronics | AFRL | **Direct** — post-silicon trusted validation | ~$3–16M range | Medium — prime/sub |
| STRATFI/TACFI | AFWERX | Bridge funding post-Phase II | $375K–$15M | Medium — needs prior Phase II |

